# React Native Development Guidelines

## Core Principles

- Use modern React Native and React patterns.
- Use functional components and hooks.
- Write TypeScript-first code.
- Prefer simple, readable solutions over unnecessary abstractions.
- Follow the existing project architecture and conventions.
- Reuse existing components, hooks, utilities, and services before creating new ones.
- Do not introduce a new library when existing project dependencies can solve the problem.
- Do not modify native iOS or Android code unless the requirement genuinely requires it.
- Keep platform-specific code isolated when possible.

## Components

- Keep components small and focused on a single responsibility.
- Prefer composition over deeply nested component hierarchies.
- Separate presentation from business logic.
- Avoid "god components" containing API calls, complex business logic, navigation, and large amounts of UI in one file.
- Extract complex logic into hooks or feature-level modules.
- Keep reusable components independent from specific screens whenever possible.

Prefer:

```tsx
function ProfileScreen() {
  const { user } = useUser();

  return (
    <Screen>
      <ProfileHeader user={user} />
      <ProfileDetails user={user} />
    </Screen>
  );
}